§ `Hand-written`

-- Section 2(1): the Ordinances in Parts 1, 2 and 3 are repealed.
#ASSERT `s 2(1), (2): what this Act does to the instrument named` "Interpretation Ordinance 1931" EQUALS JUST `repeals the instrument`
#ASSERT `s 2(1), (2): what this Act does to the instrument named` "Interpretation (Amendment) Ordinance 1978" EQUALS JUST `repeals the instrument`
#ASSERT `s 2(1), (2): what this Act does to the instrument named` "Regulations Publication Ordinance 1952" EQUALS JUST `repeals the instrument`
#ASSERT `s 2(1), (2): what this Act does to the instrument named` "Administrator's Council Ordinance 1976" EQUALS JUST `repeals the instrument`
-- Section 2(2): the South Australian laws in Part 4 cease to have effect as laws of the Northern Territory.
#ASSERT `s 2(1), (2): what this Act does to the instrument named` "The Language of Acts Amendment Act, 1900." EQUALS JUST `ends the instrument's effect in the Northern Territory as a law of the Northern Territory`
-- An instrument the Schedule does not name: the text does not say.
#ASSERT `s 2(1), (2): what this Act does to the instrument named` "Interpretation Ordinance 1999" EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 2(1), (2): what this Act does to the instrument named` "Interpretation Act 1978" EQUALS NOTHING
-- Counts, read from the Schedule: 26 Ordinances in Part 1, 2 in Part 2, 3 in Part 3 and 2 laws in Part 4: 33 in all.
#ASSERT count `instruments named in the Schedule` EQUALS 33
